Stocks ended modestly higher Thursday, gaining ground a day after equities weakened in the wake of the Federal Reserve's widely expected decision to lift interest rates and kept largely to its forecast for future increases. The S&P 500 ended 0.3% higher near 2,914, according to preliminary figures, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average gained around 55 points, or 0.2%, to end near 26,440. The tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite led the way higher, rising 0.6% toe close near 8,041.97. Shares of Apple Inc. (AAPL) paced gains for the Dow, rising 2.1%.
-MarketWatch;
 27-18 1654ET
